-- title:
--   No zero of j along the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $p \nmid N$, and write $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. Let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ be a morphism with $X$ integral and $c$ proper and smooth of relative dimension $1$. The data assumed are: a curve model $M_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ with function field the subfield `modularFunctionFieldFull N` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the expansions $j(q^d)$ for $d \mid N$, together with an isomorphism $e_0$ onto the pullback of $c$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Q} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ commuting with the projections; a section $\varepsilon_\infty$ of $c$; a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose associated place is the $q$-adic cusp `cuspInftyFull N`, and a $\mathbb{Q}$-point $y$ of the pullback lying over $\varepsilon_\infty$ and carried to $x_0$ by $e_0^{-1}$; a curve model $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field `modularFunctionFieldBar N`, isomorphic over the base to the corresponding pullback, with Galois equivariance of the point–place bijection and compatibility of the places of its $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points with the places of $M_0$ under the base-change identification; for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit in $A$, a ring map $\rho_A : \mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to A$ lifting the inclusion $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a curve model over the residue field of $A$ with function field `modularFunctionFieldFullC`, isomorphic over the base to the pullback of $c$ along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue of $\rho_A$, and, when that residue field is algebraically closed, a place map $r$ satisfying `IsPlaceReductionModL` (degree preserving and compatible with divisors of coefficientwise reduced Laurent series) through which reduction of points is computed. Finally let $s$ be a closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ such that the image of $x_0$ in $X$ specialises to $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$, let $m > 0$, and let $a, b$ be germs in the stalk of $X$ at $\varepsilon_\infty(s)$, neither lying in the ideal generated by the germ of $p$. Reading such a germ as an element of `modularFunctionFieldFull N` by specialising to $x_0$, applying the stalk map of $e_0$ followed by the first projection, passing to the function field of $M_0.C$ and applying $M_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, the conclusion is that the identity $p^m \cdot a = j(q) \cdot b$ in $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ is impossible.
--
--   This is the statement that $j$ has no zero along the special fibre of the $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-model of $X_0(N)$ near the cusp section: near $\infty_s$ the function $j$ cannot be written as $p^m a/b$ with $m > 0$ and $a, b$ germs that are units at the generic point of the special fibre. It supplies the case $m > 0$ of the trichotomy on the vertical order of $j$, and is used by [`ModularCurve.exists_notMem_span_germ_and_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_notMem_span_germ_and_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero).
-- source:
